  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NDC Transport Initiative for Asia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rapid economic growth, together with a persistent trend towards urbanization and a rise of motorized transport are leading to an increase of traffic volumes in Asia. This leads to an increase of greenhouse gas emissions and severe air pollution.  The NDC Transport Initiative for Asia, a joint program of seven organizations, promoted an integrated approach to the decarbonisation of transport. In each partner country, the initiative supported stakeholder processes and the development of measures for climate change mitigation. As a result, the project helped its partners to make their sectoral contributions to increase their NDCs, and to take a more ambitious approach to long-term strategies and the 2025 NDCs. As a regional initiative, the project shared its knowledge throughout Asia and promotes regional discourse on the need for net zero carbon transport. At the global level, the program disseminated and exchanged insights within the UNFCCC process.</narrative>
  </description>
